t-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:5ea2aebc617112bef13e32bb31e348d188892ee577eb38a753d3838b9959acc2","file":"preprints/An-explicit-counterexample-to-the-Auslander-Reiten-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex","line":26,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"24d6385c7cb21f2b043d0756b8ec50c97fc60c6218ae02f4fab03bf634805c62","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/An-explicit-counterexample-to-the-Auslander-Reiten-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5ea2aebc617112bef13e32bb31e348d188892ee577eb38a753d3838b9959acc2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-explicit-counterexample-to-the-Auslander-Reiten-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex#L26"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $\\kk=\\mathbb F_2(q,H_1,H_2)$, where $q,H_1,H_2$ are algebraically\nindependent. There exist a finite-dimensional $\\kk$-algebra $\\Lambda$\nand a finite-dimensional nonprojective left $\\Lambda$-module $Z$ such that\n\\[\n \\Ext^i_\\Lambda(Z,Z)=0=\\Ext^i_\\Lambda(Z,\\Lambda)\n \\qquad\\text{for every integer }i\\geq1.\n\\]\nThe module $Z$ is Gorenstein-projective. The semisimple quotient is\n$\\Lambda/\\rad\\Lambda\\simeq\\kk^8$, so the algebra is split with eight\nisomorphism classes of simple modules; also $\\rad(\\Lambda)^4\\ne0$.\nThese conclusions persist after every field extension of $\\kk$."}
